title: 3. Why a plan has these parts, and the example between parts
pid: 276877af-a0fb-42ab-9e68-909b62c8d67b
body: |2-
  Rests on: read (Google: alternatives considered are the most
  important part, non-goals, the 1-3 page mini design doc; Nygard's
  decision records; Oxide's states; Anthropic's research system: a
  brief needs an objective, an output, its tools and its boundaries,
  and vague briefs caused duplicated work; GitHub's spec-driven
  development: tasks small enough to check in isolation).
  First use: Libby found that the server's builder and the clients'
  would each have guessed the form of the messages between them; the
  plan then gave whole examples, and the two parts met. The state
  'being built' is from the first use too: Vic's plan needed it.
